      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the inverse functions $f^{-1}(x)$ and $g^{-1}(x)$:\n$$y = 4x - 2 \\implies x = \\frac{y + 2}{4} \\implies f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 2}{4}$$\n$$y = \\frac{4}{x + 1} \\implies x + 1 = \\frac{4}{y} \\implies g^{-1}(x) = \\frac{4}{x} - 1 = \\frac{4 - x}{x}$$",
        "Equate the two inverse functions:\n$$\\frac{x + 2}{4} = \\frac{4 - x}{x}$$",
        "Cross-multiply and form a quadratic equation in $x$:\n$$x(x + 2) = 4(4 - x) \\implies x^2 + 2x = 16 - 4x \\implies x^2 + 6x - 16 = 0$$",
        "Factorise and solve for $x$:\n$$(x + 8)(x - 2) = 0 \\implies x = 2 \\quad\\text{or}\\quad x = -8$$"
